' A record field naming a resource WITHOUT the `RES` marker.
'
' plan-114-D: this fixture used to pin `TYPE_RESOURCE_FIELD_FORBIDDEN` — records
' could not hold resources at all. They can now, so what it pins changed from a
' refusal to a correction: the field needs the ownership marker
' (`TYPE_RESOURCE_REQUIRES_RES`), exactly as a bare `List OF fs::File` element
' does. Same program rejected, actionable message instead of a flat "no".
'
' This is the fixture plan-114-D §3 calls non-optional. If the field walk had
' stopped emitting the retired ban without ROUTING to the marker rule, a bare
' unmarked resource field would be silently accepted — the escape analysis would
' not float it, and it would leak with no diagnostic at all. A test that only
' checked "2-203-0084 is gone" would have passed on that bug.
IMPORT fs

TYPE Holder
  handle AS fs::File
END TYPE

FUNC main AS Integer
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
